    <section class="detail-section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <div class="wrap detail-grid">
        <h2 id="why-title">Why should documentation be centralized?</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Product safety documentation usually consists of several materials: risk assessments, product information, supplier documents, instructions, and traceability. If information is scattered, gaps often appear only when someone asks for the material.</p>
          <h3>How does GPSRdocs help?</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Collects product-specific documents into one view.</li>
            <li>Helps identify missing attachments and open risks.</li>
            <li>Makes documentation status visible to management.</li>
            <li>Reduces dependency on individual folder structures.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

